  <prompt>Bring the SmartTodo `useLaunchContext.test.ts` suite to fully real, passing assertions (no placeholder tests) and add unit-test coverage for the FR-02/FR-03 priority/effort auto-score mappings (delivered by task 011), the FR-06 filter combination/defaults/clear-all logic (delivered by task 021), and the FR-07 Completed-toggle logic (delivered by task 022). Use the SmartTodo Code Page's EXISTING Jest harness (`src/solutions/SmartTodo/jest.config.cjs`) — do NOT introduce Vitest as a new/second runner; spec.md's "vitest" wording is stale terminology from before R4-114 wired Jest (code wins over docs per root CLAUDE.md §2).</prompt>

  <role>Spaarke platform developer. Expert in Jest + ts-jest + React Testing Library unit testing for TypeScript/React Code Pages and shared component libraries. Follow ADR-038 testing-strategy principles strictly (translated to the TS ecosystem — see constraints).</role>

  <goal>(1) `src/solutions/SmartTodo/src/hooks/__tests__/useLaunchContext.test.ts` has zero placeholder assertions (`expect(true).toBe(true)`) and its stale "no test runner wired" header comment is removed/corrected; every `it()` block in the file passes under `npm test` (Jest) in `src/solutions/SmartTodo`. (2) New coverage tests exist for the FR-02/FR-03 priority→score and effort→score mapping functions delivered by task 011, wherever task 011 places its single-source-of-truth mapping (expected: an extension of `src/client/shared/Spaarke.SmartTodo.Components/src/utils/todoScoring.ts`); if `Spaarke.SmartTodo.Components` still has no working Jest runner at that point, one is wired per the `Spaarke.UI.Components/jest.config.js` pattern, and the pre-existing orphaned `__tests__/SmartTodoWidget.test.tsx` executes and passes as a side effect. (3) New coverage tests exist for the FR-06 filter-combination/defaults/clear-all logic delivered by task 021 and the FR-07 Completed-toggle logic delivered by task 022, in the SmartTodo Code Page Jest suite. All suites green; zero ADR-038-banned test shapes introduced.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec FR-16 (TEST-1): "Bring the 22 `useLaunchContext` executable-spec shims to passing tests; add coverage for FR-02/FR-03 (auto-score mappings), FR-06 (filter combination logic, defaults, clear-all), and FR-07 (Completed toggle)." `useLaunchContext.test.ts` currently carries a 2026-06-08 header claiming "SmartTodo's package.json does NOT currently include a test runner" — that is now FALSE: R4-114 (commit history, 2026-06-25) wired `src/solutions/SmartTodo/jest.config.cjs` (ts-jest + jsdom), and `testMatch: ['**/__tests__/**/*.test.ts', '**/__tests__/**/*.test.tsx']` already picks this file up. The file's ~30+ `it()` blocks for the pure `parseLaunchContextFromSearch` parser already run for real under Jest today (the "shim" framing is stale for those). The two genuinely-unfinished tests are the final `describe('useLaunchContext hook — URL clearing side-effect (jsdom required)')` block's two `it()`s, which are literal `expect(true).toBe(true)` placeholders with a "PSEUDO-TEST" comment describing the real assertion. Separately, `Spaarke.SmartTodo.Components/__tests__/SmartTodoWidget.test.tsx` exists but the package has NO test runner at all wired (no `jest`/`vitest` devDependency, no `"test"` script) — confirmed by inspecting `package.json`. FR-02/FR-03's mapping tables are described as "the single source of truth shared by form handler + wizards + quick-add", which points at a shared-lib location (most likely `todoScoring.ts`) rather than a single call site — task 011 decides the exact location; this task adds coverage wherever it lands.</background>
