  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">MUST use Jest (the SmartTodo Code Page's existing runner, `jest.config.cjs`) for all Code-Page-side tests in this task. MUST NOT add Vitest anywhere in this task's scope — the codebase's established convention for every shared-lib + Code-Page unit-test suite (Spaarke.UI.Components, SmartTodo) is Jest + ts-jest; introducing a second runner has no cost-of-doing-nothing justification per root CLAUDE.md §11 and would fail the "prefer extending an existing service" test.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope boundary: this task ONLY adds/completes TEST coverage once 011/021/022 land. It MUST NOT implement FR-02/03/06/07 production logic itself — if a dependency task's logic is missing or not yet in a testable shape, treat that as the escalation trigger below rather than writing the production code inline.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Apply the ADR-038 §7 build-vs-maintain philosophy even though the file's literal "7 KEEP paths" taxonomy is .NET-scoped: every new test must name a concrete production behavior it protects (not a coverage-% filler); no DI-registration-only tests; no ctor/constructor null-check tests; no mirror tests (1:1 with a trivial getter/mapping); no pass-through-wrapper tests. Coverage is observation, never a gate.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Mock only at module boundaries (e.g., `Xrm.WebApi`, `@spaarke/ui-components` catalog) — do not mock the function/module under test itself. Follow the `jest.mock('@spaarke/ui-components', ...)` module-boundary pattern already used in `RegardingResolverApp.test.tsx` where an analogous boundary exists.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec">FR-16 acceptance is literally "vitest suite green" in spec.md — per root CLAUDE.md §2 (code wins, docs lag) this is interpreted as "the SmartTodo Code Page's actual Jest suite is green" (plus the shared-lib Jest suite this task wires). Document this interpretation explicitly in the task notes so the terminology drift is traceable, not silently reinterpreted.</constraint>
  </constraints>

