  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Declare 🔒 RIGOR LEVEL: FULL (test-modifying override) before starting. Load knowledge/files. Confirm tasks 011, 021, 022 are marked complete in TASK-INDEX.md; if any is not, STOP per the gate and escalate/wait rather than authoring against unfinished production code.</step>
    <step order="1">Read task 011/021/022's actual landed diffs (via git log/diff on their touched files, or the completed POML `&lt;notes&gt;` completion summaries) to find the exact functions/locations for the priority/effort mapping, the filter-combination predicate, and the Completed-toggle logic.</step>
    <step order="2">In `useLaunchContext.test.ts`: delete the stale "TEST-RUNNER STATUS (2026-06-08)" header block claiming no runner exists (Jest has run this file since R4-114); replace the two `expect(true).toBe(true)` placeholder tests in the `useLaunchContext hook — URL clearing side-effect` describe block with real assertions per their own "PSEUDO-TEST" comments — render the hook via `@testing-library/react`'s `renderHook` (add `@testing-library/react` as a SmartTodo devDependency if not already present; React 19-compatible version), seed `window.location.search`/`history`, and assert the launch params are cleared via `history.replaceState` while non-launch params (e.g. `data=...`) are preserved.</step>
    <step order="3">Run `npm test` in `src/solutions/SmartTodo`; confirm every `it()` in `useLaunchContext.test.ts` passes. Note the actual total test count in this file in task notes (spec.md cites "22"; reconcile without treating a numeric mismatch alone as a blocker).</step>
    <step order="4">Add coverage for the FR-02/FR-03 auto-score mappings at the location found in step 1 (expected: `Spaarke.SmartTodo.Components/src/utils/todoScoring.ts`). If that package still has no Jest runner, wire `jest.config.js` + `"test": "jest"` script + devDependencies (`jest`, `ts-jest`, `jest-environment-jsdom`, `@types/jest`, `identity-obj-proxy`) following `Spaarke.UI.Components/jest.config.js` exactly; confirm the pre-existing `__tests__/SmartTodoWidget.test.tsx` now executes and passes as a side effect of wiring the runner.</step>
    <step order="5">Add coverage for the FR-06 filter-combination logic at the location found in step 1: each filter category narrows the kanban predicate independently and in combination (Priority ∩ Status ∩ Due-date ∩ Assigned-To); the default filter state is Status={Open, In Progress}; Clear-all resets to that default.</step>
    <step order="6">Add coverage for the FR-07 Completed-toggle logic at the location found in step 1: Completed items are excluded from the default predicate; toggling "Show Completed" includes them; toggling off re-excludes them.</step>
    <step order="7">Run the full SmartTodo Code Page Jest suite (and the shared-lib suite if wired in step 4); confirm all green. Grep the new/changed test files for banned shapes (constructor-null-check style, DI-registration-only, trivial `expect(x).toBeDefined()` fillers) and remove any found.</step>
    <step order="8">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md`: mark 040 ✅.</step>
    <step order="9">Document any deviations (esp. the actual vs. spec-cited "22" count, and the Jest-not-Vitest interpretation of the FR-16 acceptance text) in `projects/smart-todo-r5/notes/`.</step>
  </steps>

