  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given `useLaunchContext.test.ts`, when `npm test` runs in `src/solutions/SmartTodo`, then every `it()` block in the file passes with a real assertion (zero `expect(true).toBe(true)` placeholders remain).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the FR-02/FR-03 mapping functions delivered by task 011, when their unit tests run, then Urgent/High/Medium/Low map to 100/75/50/25 and Low/Medium/High/VeryHigh/None map to 25/50/75/100/50 respectively, matching FR-02/FR-03 exactly.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the FR-06 filter logic delivered by task 021, when unit tests run, then each category (Priority/Status/Due-date/Assigned-To) narrows the predicate independently and in combination, the default state is Status={Open, In Progress}, and Clear-all resets to that default.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the FR-07 Completed-toggle logic delivered by task 022, when unit tests run, then Completed items are excluded by default and included only when the toggle is on.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: if any dependency task's logic is not in a single testable seam, the task escalates per the trigger above rather than shipping duplicated-logic tests.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">All Jest suites touched by this task (SmartTodo Code Page + Spaarke.SmartTodo.Components, if wired) pass; zero ADR-038-banned test shapes introduced (verified by self-review against the constraint list).</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Reconciles spec.md's "vitest"/"22 shims" wording against the actual Jest-based state of the repo (code wins over docs, per root CLAUDE.md §2). File the terminology drift in `notes/` rather than silently "fixing" the spec text. `Spaarke.SmartTodo.Components/package.json` currently has ONLY `"build": "tsc --noEmit"` / `"lint": "tsc --noEmit"` scripts and no test runner at all — step 4 is the first time this package gets a working unit-test story.

COMPLETION SUMMARY (2026-08-16): Since tasks 011/021/022 had already landed most of FR-02/03/06/07 coverage before this task ran, the real remaining scope was: (1) wire Jest to `Spaarke.SmartTodo.Components` via `jest.config.cjs` (`.cjs` not `.js` — package is `"type":"module"`; `roots:['<rootDir>']` not `src/` — its 3 pre-existing test files live in a top-level `__tests__/`, not nested under `src/`; no `collectCoverageFrom`/`coverageThreshold` per ADR-038 coverage-is-observation); (2) convert its 3 Jest-less `assert()`-style suites (`SmartTodoWidget.test.tsx`, `priorityEffortCardUi.test.ts`, `useKanbanColumns.test.ts` — no separate 4th file existed) to real Jest `describe`/`it`/`expect`, which surfaced and fixed genuine API drift in `SmartTodoWidget.test.tsx` (`buildSmartTodoQuery`'s param was renamed `userId`→`contactId` and its owner-clause field `_ownerid_value`→`_sprk_assignedto_value` post UAT 2026-06-20, invisible until the test actually ran); (3) fix the 2 real `expect(true).toBe(true)` placeholders in `useLaunchContext.test.ts` with real `@testing-library/react` `renderHook` assertions, correcting a second stale assumption in the process (the `data=` param is ALWAYS cleared by `clearLaunchParams`, not selectively preserved — `keysToClear` includes the literal `'data'` key unconditionally); (4) fill the one genuine FR-06 gap found — no test anywhere proved multiple Filter-pane categories combine correctly in one `$filter=` string (each was only tested in isolation) — added 2 tests to `queryHelpers.test.ts`. Final: `Spaarke.SmartTodo.Components` 27/27 passing (new), `solutions/SmartTodo` 116/116 passing (was 114/114). Both packages' `tsc` clean for files this task touched. Quality gates (code-review + adr-check) both clean, zero Critical/Warning. Discovered-but-out-of-scope: `solutions/SmartTodo/jest.config.cjs` has a pre-existing `setupFilesAfterEach` typo (should be `setupFilesAfterEnv`) that silently no-ops `jest.setup.cjs`; not fixed (outside this task's touch-list; flagged for follow-up). Full detail: `projects/smart-todo-r5/notes/task-040-test-infra.md`.</notes>

